  "description": "Idora generates prefixed, time-ordered entity identifiers such as usr_01k2f9v8ta7m3x0qbrn4dzeh5c. Each ID carries a per-entity prefix so you can tell what it identifies at a glance, followed by a lowercase ULID (default) or UUIDv7 so IDs sort by creation time and index well. Prefixes are registered once at startup, either fluently at DI setup or with an [EntityPrefix] attribute on the entity, eliminating magic strings and catching collisions at startup. IdoraId parses, validates and orders identifiers from any Idora package, and round-trips through JSON and model binding. Formerly published as UserFriendlyIds.",
